  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{32}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{32}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{32}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{32}{x}^{3/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/5+1}}{(\\frac{3}{5}+1)}{|}_{1}^{32} \\\\  & ={\\frac{5}{8}\\,{x}^{8/5}|}_{1}^{32} \\\\  & ={\\frac{5}{8}\\,(\\sqrt[5]{x})^{8}|}_{1}^{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\,((\\sqrt[5]{32})^{8}-(\\sqrt[5]{1})^{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\,({2}^{8}-{1}^{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}(256-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1275}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
